<title>JAPAN: Green Cross shares higher on banks' financial help.</title>
<headline>Green Cross shares higher on banks' financial help.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Green Cross Corp rose on Monday morning, helped by Friday's news that banks were planning to provide the pharmaceuticals maker with financial help, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0046 GMT, the shares were up 33 yen at 550 yen, on a volume of 2.278 million.</p>
<p>Sakura Bank Ltd said on Friday that it and some other banks were planning to help the drug maker.</p>
</text>
